<b>Hazama
Zetsubi</b>

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.230
<b>Banryuu
Reoko</b>

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.520
<b>Tsuwabuki
Akihito</b>

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.520
<b>Matobai
Shuusaku</b>

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.520
<b>Banryuu
Reoko</b>

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.520
<b>Arabashiri
Souya</b>

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.520
<b>Hazama
Zetsubi</b>

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.990
<b><i>Bubuki/Buranki</i></b>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:28.500
<b>Episode 10
The Shattered Heart</b>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:28.500
<b><i>Bubuki/Buranki</i></b>

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.840
We won't even get a chance 
to take the heart now.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.590
We'll never be able to 
face our elder brother...

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.770
Oh, honestly... Are none of you 
capable of doing even a single thing?

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.520
Elder Brother!

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.700
It looks like you two will 
need to be punished.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.050
You worthless gutter rats!

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.360
Bastards!

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:22.600
Have you forgotten the debt you 
owe my father for taking you in?!

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:25.010
Have you forgotten how he gave you

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:28.770
a place to live and warm soup 
to eat when you had nothing?!

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.520
How dare the right and left 
foot defy the heart?!

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.880
Damn you! Damn you!

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.140
That's right! You two 
are always so impudent.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:40.740
Y-Yeah, yeah! You both 
ought to learn your place!

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.740
Elder Brother, I'll wipe 
off the mouse's blood.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:57.250
It's not like I wanted to be 
born as someone's foot.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.380
Dersu...

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.050
Now, go and steal the heart from them.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.350
Do not humiliate me again, little sisters.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.470
Y-Yes! We understand, Elder Brother!

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:18.360
What the hell is this?!

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.410
We can do this, Azuma!

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:22.860
Time to pay you back for what 
you pulled in Kamakura!

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:30.300
It burns... It hurts!

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.350
So this is what it means to control Entei...

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:38.040
So Reoko-sama...
Reoko endured this for all that time?

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:45.010
Don't underestimate me, you brats!

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.430
That's the way, Righty-chan!

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.640
We can do this!

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.650
As we are now, we can beat Entei!

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.280
What?

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.160
Are those the Russian Bubuki users?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.120
This is it!

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:14.430
If you don't want these 
girls burned to a crisp,

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.710
hand over all the Bubuki you have!

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.080
Elder Brother! Don't do it!

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.110
Don't worry about us!

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:26.510
Fine. I'll give you all of our Bubuki.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.260
<i>Elder Brother!</i>

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:32.710
Even the priceless Bubuki I 
inherited from my parents

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:35.140
are not worth your lives.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.640
<i>Once we revive Zanpaza,</i>

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.850
<i>a clash with Entei will be inevitable.</i>

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:48.660
<i>So I might as well let it show me the full 
extent of its power, in its complete form.</i>

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.280
Entei took control of their Bubuki!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.390
Everyone, here it comes!

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:19.000
Azuma!

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:27.570
This is the power of the complete Entei,
with all its limbs!

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.410
It's magnificent!

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.240
Damn! I can't just watch this!

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:41.580
Epizo! That imbecile!

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:47.840
Azuma! There's still more 
to the power of a Buranki!

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.260
I'll teach you all the secrets 
I know about the heart!

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.680
A-chan, are you okay?

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.610
Oubu is in its complete form, too...

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:03.940
And Entei is even stronger still?

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.940
I have to finish this now.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:10.200
I can't hold out any longer.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.500
Azuma!

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.000
What? Isn't that the American...

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.370
...lardo?

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.100
Break the heart!

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.380
You have to break the heart!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.770
Huh? What'd he say?

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:29.550
What's he saying at a time like this?

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.630
Tsk! Meddling fool!

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:35.750
The heart...

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.040
Break the heart!

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.020
The Buranki's—

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:42.810
Epizo!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.810
My God!

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.820
You guys!

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:50.040
Ugh, keeping up with your 
stupidity is not easy.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.340
This is one heavy Buranki...

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:54.620
How much does that old hag weigh?

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:59.480
Ouargla, it's rude to ask a 
fat lady about her weight!

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:02.840
Why do we have to help those guys?

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:06.780
Luis, never mind the small stuff!

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:09.300
Now that we've exchanged blows,

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.550
Azuma and I are as brothers!

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.300
Azuma!

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.460
Break the heart!

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:18.810
Draw out your Buranki's true power!

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.260
Break the heart?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.450
Hey! Azuma, what are you doing?!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:32.690
Why would you listen to that idiot?

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.880
Epizo risked his life to tell me that.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:37.160
I trust him.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:40.450
You're too damn trusting.

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.160
I guess we don't have any other options.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:47.880
We can...

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:48.750
...help, too!

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.930
Okay, all together!

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.510
One, two...

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.090
Again!

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:03.350
It's working!

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.640
One, two...

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:15.990
A-chan!

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:27.620
No way! The heart went into its skull?!

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.500
Is this...

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:34.170
the inside of Oubu's head?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.900
H-Hey! Oubu's floating in the air!

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:53.650
This must be the way to 
get to Treasure Island.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:56.100
When the owner of the heart is

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.280
placed in a Buranki's skull 
and becomes its brain,

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.810
the door to the Buranki nest is opened.

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.570
Just like Reoko said!

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:08.920
Azuma! I can't let you brats 
get to the Buranki nest!

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.010
That attack just now...

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.280
Did Azuma do that?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.520
Treasure Island...

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.660
I'm finally home.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:44.990
When the heart enters the head,

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:48.070
the Buranki opens the gate to 
the place where it was born.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.500
Huh? I feel like there's something 
important I forgot to say.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.390
Let's see...

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:59.400
"1. When you break the heart and enter 
the Buranki's head, it powers up.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.010
2. The gate to Treasure Island opens.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:03.510
3. And then..."

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.340
Epizo, isn't that bad?

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:08.500
Yeah...

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:12.230
Azuma! Get out of there, now!

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:16.070
What is this?

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:23.660
Souya...

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.850
I'm taking a look at your arm.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:31.260
So it was you who pulled me out.

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:38.310
So that's the true form of a Buranki, 
with a human as its brain...

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.610
Ow...

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:45.820
Now do you see how strong 
Reoko-sama's resolve is?

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.930
Reoko takes on too much by herself.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.900
You think she'll be able to 
carry it all alone forever?

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:55.650
What does that mean?

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:56.930
Who knows?

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:59.860
I just think there are things 
a younger guy like me

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:03.270
can see that you guys can't, 
since you're Reoko-sama's age.

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:07.210
How old are you now, anyway? Thirty-six?

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:08.920
I'm 35!

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.030
I should congratulate you 
on hitting the big 4-0!

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:13.360
Shut your mouth!

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:15.770
Well, I'm gonna take off.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:17.760
Got a few things to take care of.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.670
Souya. Thanks.

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:33.560
Back there, Oubu's attack 
knocked Entei's heart loose.

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:38.070
A Buranki should stop 
moving when that happens,

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:43.060
but I continued to feel Entei's breathing.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:46.270
Why? How?

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.810
Just what is Entei?

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:08.220
<b>Incoming Call 
Hospital</b>

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:16.900
Genma...

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:21.330
This is my way of paying back a debt.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.570
This is Treasure Island?

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:32.330
The island my dad always wanted to go to...

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:00.640
Ow...

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:02.190
What happened to Azuma?

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.800
That looks bad!

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.290
A-chan! Answer me!

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:17.450
Oubu is trying to swallow Azuma.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:18.610
What?

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.510
Who's that?

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:30.190
Thank you, Oubu,

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:32.280
for protecting Azuma all this time.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.250
I know you need him,

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.500
but I'm going to take him back now.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:38.600
I'm sorry.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:07.280
Welcome home, Azuma.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.290
A-chan!

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:26.820
Azuma!

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.680
Are you all right?!

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:31.570
All right? What do you mean?

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:35.630
Azuma, you were unconscious for three days!

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:36.620
Three days?

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.380
We worried for nothing...

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:42.800
Uh-huh. Hiiragi was more 
worried than anyone.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:45.650
He soaked his pillow with tears.

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.150
Like hell I did!

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:48.770
Good morning, Azuma.

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:51.770
Mom...

00:15:58.470 --> 00:15:59.990
We finally meet again.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:21.890
Is that...

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:23.420
It's okay.

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:26.370
All the Buranki here are peaceful.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:29.920
O-Oh... They are?

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.170
This is...

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.430
A lovely view, I think...

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:39.060
A lovely view, I think.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:48.970
Migiwa-san, I came here because there's 
a favor I want to ask of you.

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:51.640
This island is one big mass of mysteries.

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:57.430
Normally, it would be impossible for 
any living thing to survive here.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:02.140
It's almost as if something is 
maintaining the island's ecosystem.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:06.250
Uh, that's not quite what I 
wanted to talk to you about...

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:10.630
Back when my family first came here,

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:13.230
we tried to catch birds and fish to eat,

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:16.010
but I could feel the island's 
shock when we did.

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.510
It was surprised when we ate potatoes, too,

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:21.790
but there was little else we could do.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:26.600
Oh, but you kids don't need to worry.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:29.020
Eat all you like.

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:31.120
O-Okay...

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:38.250
Migiwa-san, to continue what 
I was saying before...

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:39.410
I want you to—

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.200
Here.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:43.200
Th-Thank you.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:08.820
Migiwa-san?

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.190
Oh, you're in here, Hiiragi?

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:14.610
You've really changed, you know?

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.440
All this time...

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:23.950
All this time, I wanted to ask Migiwa-san to 
come back to Earth and fight Reoko with us.

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:26.690
Yeah, that's what you were always after.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:28.420
I also wanted to ask her

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:32.860
why she abandoned Earth, 
and my dad, to come here.

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:36.900
But after working in the fields and stuff,

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:39.340
I didn't care about any of that anymore.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.730
That's the great thing about you.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.850
Huh? What does that mean?

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:46.640
Good question.

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.920
Hey, listen, Kinoa...

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.800
Did you... I mean...

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:02.920
Do it... with that Arabashiri guy?

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.120
O-Of course not!

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:08.120
Oh... You didn't?

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:11.550
But did you... k-kiss him?

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:13.630
A-Are you stupid?!

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:21.390
So she did kiss him...

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:28.030
Goodnight, Kogane-chan.

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:30.900
Oh... Yeah. Goodnight.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.740
Treasure Island is up so high,

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:47.560
but it's not cold at all.

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:52.810
So your mom is going to stay here, after all?

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.170
I see...

00:19:57.060 --> 00:20:02.380
Hey, you know, I really love 
this Treasure Island place.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.510
It seems so kind and welcoming.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.880
So this is where you grew up, huh?

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:14.700
I'm sure my dad would've loved it, too.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:19.260
A-chan, thanks for bringing me here.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:22.660
No, I was only able to come here

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:24.960
because I ran into you that day.

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:27.660
So I should thank you.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:50.020
Now my Buranki, Zanpaza, 
will be resurrected!

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:55.420
What a bore. No challenge at all.

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:59.880
I think the déraciné 
gang here is half-asleep.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:01.240
Why? Why?

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:04.600
We can't let the other Buranki 
teams get ahead of us.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:07.160
We're going after the heart, too, Epizo.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.320
Hmph! I don't think so!

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:14.090
What kind of coward takes the 
heart from a sleeping Buranki?

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:16.710
Oh?

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:18.300
Gulp!

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:26.470
What's that sound?

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:28.250
Mom!

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.010
Azuma, what is this?

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:32.350
The forest!

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:43.140
This is a much nicer place than I thought.

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:46.360
I expected it to be like Hell!

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:49.480
Arabashiri? How did you get here?!

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:53.160
You guys opened the door for me.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:55.710
I only followed you here.

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:59.150
Looks like the teams from those 
other countries are here, too.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:03.460
This is getting so exciting, 
it's almost like a festival!

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:08.190
And now it's time for a 
nice, fun Buranki hunt!
